## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design cross-tenant observability with strict data isolation, covering tracing, logging, sampling, and validation.

## Key Concepts

- OpenTelemetry and trace propagation
- Tenant isolation and boundary enforcement
- Per-tenant sampling and data redaction
- Validation in a single-namespace scenario

## Code Example

```javascript
// PII redaction example (logs)
function redactLogEvent(event, tenantId) {
  const safe = {...event};
  if (safe.message) safe.message = safe.message.replace(/\b(email|ssn|password)\b[^:]*: [^,]+/gi, 'PII_REDACTED');
  if (safe.user && safe.user.id) safe.user.id = 'REDACTED';
  return safe;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you detect and remediate cross-tenant leakage in traces?
- What metrics would you surface to confirm per-tenant isolation is preserved during incidents?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design scalable, isolated QoS for multi-tenant CNFs with real-time config updates.

## Key Concepts
- Hierarchical token bucket, per-tenant and per-path
- Dynamic priority scheduling and cross-tenant isolation
- Fast policy propagation and SLA metrics
- Kubernetes manifests and minimal tests

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo token bucket checker
class TB {
  constructor(cap, ref) { this.cap = cap; this.refill = ref; }
  consume(n=1){ if(this.cap>=n){ this.cap-=n; return true;} return false; }
  refillAt(now){ this.cap = Math.min(this.max, this.cap + (now-this.last)*this.fillRate); }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test SLA adherence under bursty traffic?
- How would you roll out policy changes safely across clusters?
